<p>Late question is very late, but still.<br />
Is there a behind the scenes type reason that a birb found down in New Mexico is hella into Haida rituals despite the sizeable distances involved?</p>
<p>I know they traveled and traded, so the mask being found afar maybe isn't the hugest leap of logic, but the bird knowing their rituals&#8230; Is it supposed to imply that they traded away a mask containing the spirit of the bird?<br />
That feels like a big thing to trade away. I'm not an expert but it seems like it's pulling multiple very differently located tribal traditions together, in a way that's not lining up with what I can see about them online at least.</p>

